IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter XIV (ss 350-356): CLOSE CORPORATIONS -- agreements
-- restricting the directors, management by the stockholders, custodians and provisional directors, the stockholders'
-- option to dissolve, and the savings clause. Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone (src:1741-1780).
-- (ss 341-349 are in dg10-close-status.l4.)
--
-- Quote lines are slices of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text): `-- src:N | ...` is line N.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation: here, a stockholder of a close
-- corporation (a party to a stockholders' agreement, an applicant for a custodian or a provisional director, or the
-- holder of an option to dissolve), a director, or a provisional director.

§ `Subchapter XIV. Close Corporations; Special Provisions (continued)`

§§ `s 350 Agreements restricting discretion of directors`

-- A written agreement among the stockholders of a close corporation holding a majority of the outstanding stock
-- entitled to vote, whether solely among themselves or with a party not a stockholder. Votes, not shares (s 212(a)).
-- src:1743 | A written agreement among the stockholders of a close corporation holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote, whether solely among themselves or with a party not a stockholder, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 350 (src:1743)
GIVEN `the agreement is a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350 the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` `the agreement is a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation` `the number of votes held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation`
    THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the number of votes held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "is not invalid, as between the parties to the agreement, on the ground that it so relates to the conduct of the
-- business and affairs of the corporation as to restrict or interfere with the discretion or powers of the board of
-- directors." Outside the section the question is not answered here (NOTHING).
-- src:1743 | is not invalid, as between the parties to the agreement, on the ground that it so relates to the conduct of the business and affairs of the corporation as to restrict or interfere with the discretion or powers of the board of directors. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 350 (src:1743)
GIVEN `the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350 the agreement is invalid, as between the parties, on the ground that it restricts or interferes with the discretion or powers of the board` `the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- "The effect of any such agreement shall be to relieve the directors and impose upon the stockholders who are
-- parties to the agreement the liability for managerial acts or omissions which is imposed on directors to the extent
-- and so long as the discretion or powers of the board in its management of corporate affairs is controlled by such
-- agreement." (fork F14: "to the extent" is a matter of degree; it is taken here as whether, at the time asked about,
-- the board's discretion is controlled by the agreement.)
-- src:1743 | The effect of any such agreement shall be to relieve the directors and impose upon the stockholders who are parties to the agreement the liability for managerial acts or omissions which is imposed on directors to the extent and so long as the discretion or powers of the board in its management of corporate affairs is controlled by such agreement.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 350 (src:1743)
GIVEN `the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the discretion or powers of the board in its management of corporate affairs is controlled by the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350 the stockholders who are parties bear the liability for managerial acts or omissions that is imposed on directors, and the directors are relieved` `the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` `the discretion or powers of the board in its management of corporate affairs is controlled by the agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN (IF `the discretion or powers of the board in its management of corporate affairs is controlled by the agreement` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 351 Management by stockholders`

-- src:1747 | The certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that the business of the corporation shall be managed by the stockholders of the corporation rather than by a board of directors. So long as this provision continues in effect:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 351 (src:1747)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation provides that the business of the corporation shall be managed by the stockholders rather than by a board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 351 the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` `the certificate of incorporation provides that the business of the corporation shall be managed by the stockholders rather than by a board of directors` MEANS
    `the certificate of incorporation provides that the business of the corporation shall be managed by the stockholders rather than by a board of directors`

-- (1): "So long as this provision continues in effect: No meeting of stockholders need be called to elect directors".
-- src:1748 | (1) No meeting of stockholders need be called to elect directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 351(1) (src:1748)
GIVEN `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(1) a meeting of stockholders must be called to elect directors` `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` MEANS
    IF `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): "Unless the context clearly requires otherwise, the stockholders of the corporation shall be deemed to be
-- directors for purposes of applying provisions of this chapter". Whether the context clearly requires otherwise is a
-- judgment the text leaves to whoever applies the provision, so it is an input (fork F15).
-- src:1749 | (2) Unless the context clearly requires otherwise, the stockholders of the corporation shall be deemed to be directors for purposes of applying provisions of this chapter; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 351(2) (src:1749)
GIVEN `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context clearly requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(2) the stockholders are deemed to be directors for purposes of applying the provision of this chapter` `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` `the context clearly requires otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the context clearly requires otherwise`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1750 | (3) The stockholders of the corporation shall be subject to all liabilities of directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 351(3) (src:1750)
GIVEN `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(3) the stockholders are subject to all liabilities of directors` `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` MEANS
    IF `the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Insertion by amendment: all incorporators and subscribers, or all holders of record of all of the outstanding stock
-- whether or not having voting power, authorize it.
-- src:1751 | Such a provision may be inserted in the certificate of incorporation by amendment if all incorporators and subscribers or all holders of record of all of the outstanding stock, whether or not having voting power, authorize such a provision. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 351 (src:1751)
GIVEN `all incorporators and subscribers authorize the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all holders of record of all of the outstanding stock, whether or not having voting power, authorize the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 351 the provision may be inserted in the certificate of incorporation by amendment` `all incorporators and subscribers authorize the provision` `all holders of record of all of the outstanding stock, whether or not having voting power, authorize the provision` MEANS
        `all incorporators and subscribers authorize the provision`
    OR  `all holders of record of all of the outstanding stock, whether or not having voting power, authorize the provision`

-- Deletion: a vote of the holders of a majority of all outstanding stock, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote.
-- src:1751 | An amendment to the certificate of incorporation to delete such a provision shall be adopted by a vote of the holders of a majority of all outstanding stock of the corporation, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 351 (src:1751)
GIVEN `the number of votes held by the holders who voted for the amendment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of all outstanding stock, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351 the amendment deleting the provision is adopted` `the number of votes held by the holders who voted for the amendment` `the number of votes of all outstanding stock, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "all outstanding stock of the corporation, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote")) `the number of votes held by the holders who voted for the amendment` `the number of votes of all outstanding stock, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote`

-- src:1751 | If the certificate of incorporation contains a provision authorized by this section, the existence of such provision shall be noted conspicuously on the face or back of every stock certificate issued by such corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 351 (src:1751)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation contains a provision authorized by s 351` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the existence of the provision is noted conspicuously on the face or back of the stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 351 the stock certificate meets the requirement to note the provision` `the certificate of incorporation contains a provision authorized by s 351` `the existence of the provision is noted conspicuously on the face or back of the stock certificate` MEANS
        (NOT `the certificate of incorporation contains a provision authorized by s 351`)
    OR  `the existence of the provision is noted conspicuously on the face or back of the stock certificate`

§§ `s 352 Appointment of custodian for close corporation`

-- src:1756 | (1) Pursuant to § 351 of this title the business and affairs of the corporation are managed by the stockholders and they are so divided that the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury and any remedy with respect to such deadlock provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws or in any written agreement of the stockholders has failed; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 352(a)(1) (src:1756)
GIVEN `the business and affairs of the corporation are managed by the stockholders under s 351` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholders are so divided that the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any remedy for the deadlock provided in the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a written agreement of the stockholders has failed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 352(a)(1) the business is deadlocked and the remedies provided have failed` `the business and affairs of the corporation are managed by the stockholders under s 351` `the stockholders are so divided that the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury` `any remedy for the deadlock provided in the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a written agreement of the stockholders has failed` MEANS
        `the business and affairs of the corporation are managed by the stockholders under s 351`
    AND `the stockholders are so divided that the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury`
    AND `any remedy for the deadlock provided in the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a written agreement of the stockholders has failed`

-- src:1757 | (2) The petitioning stockholder has the right to the dissolution of the corporation under a provision of the certificate of incorporation permitted by § 355 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 352(a)(2) (src:1757)
GIVEN `the petitioning stockholder has the right to the dissolution of the corporation under a provision of the certificate of incorporation permitted by s 355` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 352(a)(2) the petitioning stockholder has a right to dissolution under a provision permitted by s 355` `the petitioning stockholder has the right to the dissolution of the corporation under a provision of the certificate of incorporation permitted by s 355` MEANS
    `the petitioning stockholder has the right to the dissolution of the corporation under a provision of the certificate of incorporation permitted by s 355`

-- src:1755 | (a) In addition to § 226 of this title respecting the appointment of a custodian for any corporation, the Court of Chancery, upon application of any stockholder, may appoint 1 or more persons to be custodians, and, if the corporation is insolvent, to be receivers, of any close corporation when:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 352(a) (src:1755)
DECLARE `s 352(a) Appointment the Court of Chancery may make for a close corporation` IS ONE OF
    `no appointment under s 352(a)`
    `1 or more custodians under s 352(a)`
    `1 or more custodians, and, the corporation being insolvent, receivers, under s 352(a)`

-- "upon application of any stockholder ... when: (1) ... or (2) ...". The Court "may": it has the power; the text
-- does not say it must. The decision to appoint is the Court's.
-- src:1755 | (a) In addition to § 226 of this title respecting the appointment of a custodian for any corporation, the Court of Chancery, upon application of any stockholder, may appoint 1 or more persons to be custodians, and, if the corporation is insolvent, to be receivers, of any close corporation when:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 352(a) (src:1755)
GIVEN `the application is by a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground in s 352(a)(1) exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground in s 352(a)(2) exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 352(a) Appointment the Court of Chancery may make for a close corporation`
`s 352(a) the appointment the Court of Chancery may make on the application` `the application is by a stockholder` `the ground in s 352(a)(1) exists` `the ground in s 352(a)(2) exists` `the corporation is insolvent` MEANS
    IF `the application is by a stockholder` AND (`the ground in s 352(a)(1) exists` OR `the ground in s 352(a)(2) exists`)
    THEN (IF `the corporation is insolvent`
          THEN `1 or more custodians, and, the corporation being insolvent, receivers, under s 352(a)`
          ELSE `1 or more custodians under s 352(a)`)
    ELSE `no appointment under s 352(a)`

-- (b): "In lieu of appointing a custodian ... under this section or s 226 of this title the Court of Chancery may
-- appoint a provisional director ... if the Court determines that it would be in the best interest of the corporation."
-- src:1758 | In lieu of appointing a custodian for a close corporation under this section or § 226 of this title the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director, whose powers and status shall be as provided in § 353 of this title if the Court determines that it would be in the best interest of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 352(b) (src:1758)
GIVEN `a custodian could be appointed under s 352(a) or s 226` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 226 (piece dg4)
      `the Court of Chancery determines that appointing a provisional director would be in the best interest of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 352(b) the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director in lieu of a custodian` `a custodian could be appointed under s 352(a) or s 226` `the Court of Chancery determines that appointing a provisional director would be in the best interest of the corporation` MEANS
        `a custodian could be appointed under s 352(a) or s 226`
    AND `the Court of Chancery determines that appointing a provisional director would be in the best interest of the corporation`

-- "Such appointment shall not preclude any subsequent order of the Court appointing a custodian for such corporation."
-- src:1758 | Such appointment shall not preclude any subsequent order of the Court appointing a custodian for such corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 352(b) (src:1758)
GIVEN `a provisional director has been appointed under s 352(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 352(b) the appointment of the provisional director precludes a subsequent order appointing a custodian` `a provisional director has been appointed under s 352(b)` MEANS
    IF `a provisional director has been appointed under s 352(b)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 353 Appointment of a provisional director in certain cases`

-- (a): "Notwithstanding any contrary provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws or agreement of the
-- stockholders", so no input about such a provision is read.
-- src:1762 | (a) Notwithstanding any contrary provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws or agreement of the stockholders, the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director for a close corporation if the directors are so divided respecting the management of the corporation’s business and affairs that the votes required for action by the board of directors cannot be obtained with the consequence that the business and affairs of the corporation can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(a) (src:1762)
GIVEN `the corporation is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are so divided respecting the management of the corporation's business and affairs that the votes required for action by the board cannot be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a consequence the business and affairs of the corporation can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 353(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director` `the corporation is a close corporation` `the directors are so divided respecting the management of the corporation's business and affairs that the votes required for action by the board cannot be obtained` `as a consequence the business and affairs of the corporation can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally` MEANS
        `the corporation is a close corporation`
    AND `the directors are so divided respecting the management of the corporation's business and affairs that the votes required for action by the board cannot be obtained`
    AND `as a consequence the business and affairs of the corporation can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally`

-- (b): who may apply -- (1) at least one half of the directors then in office, (2) holders of at least one third of all
-- stock then entitled to elect directors, or (3) if more than 1 class is so entitled, holders of two thirds of the
-- stock of any such class. The limbs are alternatives (fork F16); the certificate of a close corporation may provide
-- a lesser proportion of the directors, of the stockholders or of a class, which then replaces the statutory one.
-- src:1763 | (b) An application for relief under this section must be filed (1) by at least one half of the number of directors then in office, (2) by the holders of at least one third of all stock then entitled to elect directors, or, (3) if there be more than 1 class of stock then entitled to elect 1 or more directors, by the holders of two thirds of the stock of any such class; but the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that a lesser proportion of the directors or of the stockholders or of a class of stockholders may apply for relief under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(b) (src:1763)
DECLARE `s 353(b) Application for a provisional director` HAS
    `the number of directors who join in the application`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the number of directors then in office`                                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the number of shares held by the stockholders who join in the application`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the number of shares then entitled to elect directors`                                                        IS A NUMBER
    `more than 1 class of stock is then entitled to elect directors`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of shares of the class in which the applicants hold the largest proportion that they hold`        IS A NUMBER
    `the number of shares of that class`                                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the lesser proportion of the directors that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one`       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the lesser proportion of the stockholders that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the lesser proportion of a class that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- src:1763 | but the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that a lesser proportion of the directors or of the stockholders or of a class of stockholders may apply for relief under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(b) (src:1763)
GIVEN `the proportion the statute requires` IS A NUMBER
      `the lesser proportion the certificate allows, if it allows one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 353(b) the proportion required to apply` `the proportion the statute requires` `the lesser proportion the certificate allows, if it allows one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the lesser proportion the certificate allows, if it allows one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the proportion the statute requires`
    WHEN JUST lesser THEN (IF lesser LESS THAN `the proportion the statute requires` THEN lesser ELSE `the proportion the statute requires`)

-- src:1763 | (1) by at least one half of the number of directors then in office, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(b) (src:1763)
GIVEN application IS A `s 353(b) Application for a provisional director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(b)(1) at least one half of the directors then in office join in the application` application MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`at least` (`s 353(b) the proportion required to apply` (1 DIVIDED BY 2) (application's `the lesser proportion of the directors that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one`)) `of` `the directors then in office`) (application's `the number of directors who join in the application`) (application's `the number of directors then in office`)

-- src:1763 | (2) by the holders of at least one third of all stock then entitled to elect directors, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(b) (src:1763)
GIVEN application IS A `s 353(b) Application for a provisional director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(b)(2) holders of at least one third of all stock then entitled to elect directors join in the application` application MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`at least` (`s 353(b) the proportion required to apply` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) (application's `the lesser proportion of the stockholders that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one`)) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "all stock then entitled to elect directors")) (application's `the number of shares held by the stockholders who join in the application`) (application's `the number of shares then entitled to elect directors`)

-- src:1763 | (3) if there be more than 1 class of stock then entitled to elect 1 or more directors, by the holders of two thirds of the stock of any such class; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(b) (src:1763)
GIVEN application IS A `s 353(b) Application for a provisional director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(b)(3) holders of two thirds of the stock of a class entitled to elect directors join in the application` application MEANS
    IF application's `more than 1 class of stock is then entitled to elect directors`
    THEN `the vote carries` (`at least` (`s 353(b) the proportion required to apply` (2 DIVIDED BY 3) (application's `the lesser proportion of a class that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one`)) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "the stock of a class then entitled to elect directors")) (application's `the number of shares of the class in which the applicants hold the largest proportion that they hold`) (application's `the number of shares of that class`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The limbs are alternatives. TRUE if either holds, else NOT COVERED if either is not covered, else FALSE.
-- src:1763 | (b) An application for relief under this section must be filed (1) by at least one half of the number of directors then in office, (2) by the holders of at least one third of all stock then entitled to elect directors, or, (3) if there be more than 1 class of stock then entitled to elect 1 or more directors, by the holders of two thirds of the stock of any such class; but the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that a lesser proportion of the directors or of the stockholders or of a class of stockholders may apply for relief under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(b) (src:1763)
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      second IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(b) either limb holds` first second MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN second
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        (CONSIDER second
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING)

-- src:1763 | (b) An application for relief under this section must be filed (1) by at least one half of the number of directors then in office, (2) by the holders of at least one third of all stock then entitled to elect directors, or, (3) if there be more than 1 class of stock then entitled to elect 1 or more directors, by the holders of two thirds of the stock of any such class; but the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that a lesser proportion of the directors or of the stockholders or of a class of stockholders may apply for relief under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(b) (src:1763)
GIVEN application IS A `s 353(b) Application for a provisional director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(b) the application may be filed` application MEANS
    `s 353(b) either limb holds` (`s 353(b) either limb holds` (`s 353(b)(1) at least one half of the directors then in office join in the application` application) (`s 353(b)(2) holders of at least one third of all stock then entitled to elect directors join in the application` application)) (`s 353(b)(3) holders of two thirds of the stock of a class entitled to elect directors join in the application` application)

-- (c): "an impartial person who is neither a stockholder nor a creditor of the corporation or of any subsidiary or
-- affiliate of the corporation, and whose further qualifications, if any, may be determined by the Court". The
-- phrase "of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate" is read as governing both "stockholder" and
-- "creditor" (fork F33).
-- src:1764 | A provisional director shall be an impartial person who is neither a stockholder nor a creditor of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation, and whose further qualifications, if any, may be determined by the Court of Chancery. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(c) (src:1764)
GIVEN `the person is impartial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a stockholder of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a creditor of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the further qualifications, if any, that the Court of Chancery determines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 353(c) the person may be appointed a provisional director` `the person is impartial` `the person is a stockholder of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation` `the person is a creditor of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation` `the person meets the further qualifications, if any, that the Court of Chancery determines` MEANS
        `the person is impartial`
    AND (NOT `the person is a stockholder of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation`)
    AND (NOT `the person is a creditor of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation`)
    AND `the person meets the further qualifications, if any, that the Court of Chancery determines`

-- src:1764 | A provisional director is not a receiver of the corporation and does not have the title and powers of a custodian or receiver appointed under §§ 226 and 291 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(c) (src:1764)
GIVEN `the person is a provisional director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(c) the provisional director has the title and powers of a custodian or receiver` `the person is a provisional director` MEANS
    IF `the person is a provisional director` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Removal: "removed by order of the Court of Chancery or by the holders of a majority of all shares then entitled to
-- vote to elect directors or by the holders of two thirds of the shares of that class of voting shares which filed
-- the application". Votes, not shares (s 212(a)).
-- src:1764 | A provisional director shall have all the rights and powers of a duly elected director of the corporation, including the right to notice of and to vote at meetings of directors, until such time as such person shall be removed by order of the Court of Chancery or by the holders of a majority of all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors or by the holders of two thirds of the shares of that class of voting shares which filed the application for appointment of a provisional director. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(c) (src:1764)
GIVEN `the Court of Chancery has ordered the provisional director removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes of the holders who voted to remove, among all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the application was filed by the holders of a class of voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes of the holders who voted to remove, among the class of voting shares which filed the application` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the class of voting shares which filed the application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(c) the provisional director is removed` `the Court of Chancery has ordered the provisional director removed` `the number of votes of the holders who voted to remove, among all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors` `the number of votes of all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors` `the application was filed by the holders of a class of voting shares` `the number of votes of the holders who voted to remove, among the class of voting shares which filed the application` `the number of votes of the class of voting shares which filed the application` MEANS
    `s 353(b) either limb holds`
        (`s 353(b) either limb holds`
            (JUST `the Court of Chancery has ordered the provisional director removed`)
            (`the vote carries` (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors")) `the number of votes of the holders who voted to remove, among all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors` `the number of votes of all shares then entitled to vote to elect directors`))
        (IF `the application was filed by the holders of a class of voting shares`
         THEN `the vote carries` (`at least` (2 DIVIDED BY 3) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "the shares of the class of voting shares which filed the application")) `the number of votes of the holders who voted to remove, among the class of voting shares which filed the application` `the number of votes of the class of voting shares which filed the application`
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- Until removed, the provisional director has all the rights and powers of a duly elected director, including the
-- right to notice of and to vote at meetings of directors.
-- src:1764 | A provisional director shall have all the rights and powers of a duly elected director of the corporation, including the right to notice of and to vote at meetings of directors, until such time as such person shall be removed …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(c) (src:1764)
GIVEN `the person is a provisional director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisional director has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(c) the provisional director has all the rights and powers of a duly elected director, including notice of and a vote at meetings of directors` `the person is a provisional director` `the provisional director has been removed` MEANS
    IF `the person is a provisional director` THEN JUST (NOT `the provisional director has been removed`) ELSE NOTHING

-- Compensation: by agreement between the provisional director and the corporation, subject to the approval of the
-- Court; the Court may fix it in the absence of agreement or in the event of disagreement.
-- src:1764 | A provisional director’s compensation shall be determined by agreement between such person and the corporation subject to approval of the Court of Chancery, which may fix such person’s compensation in the absence of agreement or in the event of disagreement between the provisional director and the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(c) (src:1764)
DECLARE `s 353(c) How the provisional director's compensation is determined` IS ONE OF
    `by the agreement between the provisional director and the corporation, approved by the Court of Chancery under s 353(c)`
    `by the agreement between the provisional director and the corporation, which the Court of Chancery has not yet approved under s 353(c)`
    `as the Court of Chancery may fix it under s 353(c), there being no agreement or the parties disagreeing`

-- src:1764 | A provisional director’s compensation shall be determined by agreement between such person and the corporation subject to approval of the Court of Chancery, which may fix such person’s compensation in the absence of agreement or in the event of disagreement between the provisional director and the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(c) (src:1764)
GIVEN `the provisional director and the corporation have agreed the compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Chancery has approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 353(c) How the provisional director's compensation is determined`
`s 353(c) the provisional director's compensation is determined` `the provisional director and the corporation have agreed the compensation` `the Court of Chancery has approved the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the provisional director and the corporation have agreed the compensation`
    THEN (IF `the Court of Chancery has approved the agreement`
          THEN `by the agreement between the provisional director and the corporation, approved by the Court of Chancery under s 353(c)`
          ELSE `by the agreement between the provisional director and the corporation, which the Court of Chancery has not yet approved under s 353(c)`)
    ELSE `as the Court of Chancery may fix it under s 353(c), there being no agreement or the parties disagreeing`

-- (d): the Court may appoint although (b) is not satisfied if s 352(b) permits.
-- src:1765 | (d) Even though the requirements of subsection (b) of this section relating to the number of directors or stockholders who may petition for appointment of a provisional director are not satisfied, the Court of Chancery may nevertheless appoint a provisional director if permitted by § 352(b) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353(d) (src:1765)
GIVEN `s 352(b) permits the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 353(d) the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director although the requirements of subsection (b) are not satisfied` `s 352(b) permits the appointment` MEANS
    `s 352(b) permits the appointment`

-- The Court's power on an application: subsection (a), and the application is one (b) allows or (d) permits.
-- src:1762 | (a) Notwithstanding any contrary provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws or agreement of the stockholders, the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director for a close corporation if the directors are so divided respecting the management of the corporation’s business and affairs that the votes required for action by the board of directors cannot be obtained with the consequence that the business and affairs of the corporation can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally.
-- src:1765 | (d) Even though the requirements of subsection (b) of this section relating to the number of directors or stockholders who may petition for appointment of a provisional director are not satisfied, the Court of Chancery may nevertheless appoint a provisional director if permitted by § 352(b) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 353 (src:1762-1765)
GIVEN `the court may appoint under s 353(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application may be filed under s 353(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 352(b) permits the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353 the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director on the application` `the court may appoint under s 353(a)` `the application may be filed under s 353(b)` `s 352(b) permits the appointment` MEANS
    IF `the court may appoint under s 353(a)`
    THEN `s 353(b) either limb holds` `the application may be filed under s 353(b)` (JUST (`s 353(d) the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director although the requirements of subsection (b) are not satisfied` `s 352(b) permits the appointment`))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 354 Operating corporation as partnership`

-- src:1769 | No written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation, nor any provision of the certificate of incorporation or of the bylaws of the corporation, which agreement or provision relates to any phase of the affairs of such corporation, including but not limited to the management of its business or declaration and payment of dividends or other division of profits or the election of directors or officers or the employment of stockholders by the corporation or the arbitration of disputes, shall be invalid on the ground that it is an attempt by the parties to the agreement or by the stockholders of the corporation to treat the corporation as if it were a partnership or to arrange relations among the stockholders or between the stockholders and the corporation in a manner that would be appropriate only among partners.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 354 (src:1769)
DECLARE `s 354 Instrument of a close corporation` IS ONE OF
    `a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation under s 354`
    `a provision of the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation under s 354`
    `a provision of the bylaws of a close corporation under s 354`
    `an instrument that s 354 does not name`

-- The instrument is not invalid on the ground that it is an attempt to treat the corporation as a partnership or to
-- arrange relations among the stockholders, or between them and the corporation, in a way appropriate only among
-- partners. An instrument the section does not name is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:1769 | No written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation, nor any provision of the certificate of incorporation or of the bylaws of the corporation, which agreement or provision relates to any phase of the affairs of such corporation, including but not limited to the management of its business or declaration and payment of dividends or other division of profits or the election of directors or officers or the employment of stockholders by the corporation or the arbitration of disputes, shall be invalid on the ground that it is an attempt by the parties to the agreement or by the stockholders of the corporation to treat the corporation as if it were a partnership or to arrange relations among the stockholders or between the stockholders and the corporation in a manner that would be appropriate only among partners.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 354 (src:1769)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 354 Instrument of a close corporation`
      `the instrument relates to a phase of the affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 354 the instrument is invalid on the ground that it treats the corporation as a partnership` instrument `the instrument relates to a phase of the affairs of the corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `an instrument that s 354 does not name` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE (IF `the instrument relates to a phase of the affairs of the corporation` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING)

§§ `s 355 Stockholders' option to dissolve corporation`

-- (c) first: the stock certificate must conspicuously note on its face the existence of the provision; "Unless noted
-- conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate, the provision is ineffective." (fork F17: read as ineffective
-- as to the holder of a stock certificate that does not note it.)
-- src:1775 | (c) Each stock certificate in any corporation whose certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by this section shall conspicuously note on the face thereof the existence of the provision. Unless noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate, the provision is ineffective.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(c) (src:1775)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 355(c) the stock certificate meets the requirement to note the provision` `the certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate` MEANS
        (NOT `the certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355`)
    OR  `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate`

-- src:1775 | (c) Each stock certificate in any corporation whose certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by this section shall conspicuously note on the face thereof the existence of the provision. Unless noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate, the provision is ineffective.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(c) (src:1775)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355(c) the provision is effective as to the holder of the stock certificate` `the certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355`
    THEN JUST `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (a): the option, who may exercise it, when, and with what effect.
-- src:1773 | (a) The certificate of incorporation of any close corporation may include a provision granting to any stockholder, or to the holders of any specified number or percentage of shares of any class of stock, an option to have the corporation dissolved at will or upon the occurrence of any specified event or contingency. Whenever any such option to dissolve is exercised, the stockholders exercising such option shall give written notice thereof to all other stockholders. After the expiration of 30 days following the sending of such notice, the dissolution of the corporation shall proceed as if the required number of stockholders having voting power had consented in writing to dissolution of the corporation as provided by § 228 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(a) (src:1773)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation includes a provision granting an option to have the corporation dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a stockholder, or with others holds the number or percentage of shares of a class that the provision specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the option is at will, or the event or contingency the provision specifies has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 355(a) the option to have the corporation dissolved may be exercised` `the certificate of incorporation includes a provision granting an option to have the corporation dissolved` `the person is a stockholder, or with others holds the number or percentage of shares of a class that the provision specifies` `the option is at will, or the event or contingency the provision specifies has occurred` `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate` MEANS
        `the certificate of incorporation includes a provision granting an option to have the corporation dissolved`
    AND `the person is a stockholder, or with others holds the number or percentage of shares of a class that the provision specifies`
    AND `the option is at will, or the event or contingency the provision specifies has occurred`
    AND `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate`

-- "Whenever any such option to dissolve is exercised, the stockholders exercising such option shall give written
-- notice thereof to all other stockholders."
-- src:1773 | Whenever any such option to dissolve is exercised, the stockholders exercising such option shall give written notice thereof to all other stockholders. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(a) (src:1773)
GIVEN `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given to all other stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 355(a) the notice of the exercise of the option meets the subsection` `the notice is in writing` `the notice is given to all other stockholders` MEANS
    `the notice is in writing` AND `the notice is given to all other stockholders`

-- "After the expiration of 30 days following the sending of such notice, the dissolution of the corporation shall
-- proceed": the first day on which it proceeds is the day after the 30th day (fork F18).
-- src:1773 | After the expiration of 30 days following the sending of such notice, the dissolution of the corporation shall proceed as if the required number of stockholders having voting power had consented in writing to dissolution of the corporation as provided by § 228 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(a) (src:1773)
GIVEN `the date the notice was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 355(a) the first day on which the dissolution proceeds` `the date the notice was sent` MEANS
    (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` `the date the notice was sent`) PLUS 1

-- src:1773 | After the expiration of 30 days following the sending of such notice, the dissolution of the corporation shall proceed as if the required number of stockholders having voting power had consented in writing to dissolution of the corporation as provided by § 228 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(a) (src:1773)
GIVEN `the option was exercised in accordance with s 355(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of the exercise meets s 355(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 355(a) the dissolution proceeds as if the required stockholders had consented in writing under s 228` `the option was exercised in accordance with s 355(a)` `the notice of the exercise meets s 355(a)` `the date the notice was sent` `the date asked about` MEANS
        `the option was exercised in accordance with s 355(a)`
    AND `the notice of the exercise meets s 355(a)`
    AND `the date asked about` AT LEAST (`s 355(a) the first day on which the dissolution proceeds` `the date the notice was sent`)

-- (b): adding the provision by amendment: the affirmative vote of the holders of all the outstanding stock, whether
-- or not entitled to vote, unless the certificate specifically authorizes such an amendment by a vote not less than
-- 2/3 of all the outstanding stock whether or not entitled to vote (fork F19: a figure in the certificate below 2/3
-- is not an authorization the section allows, so all the stock must vote for it).
-- src:1774 | (b) If the certificate of incorporation as originally filed does not contain a provision authorized by subsection (a) of this section, the certificate may be amended to include such provision if adopted by the affirmative vote of the holders of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote, unless the certificate of incorporation specifically authorizes such an amendment by a vote which shall be not less than 2/3 of all the outstanding stock whether or not entitled to vote.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(b) (src:1774)
GIVEN `the proportion of all the outstanding stock by which the certificate specifically authorizes such an amendment, if it does` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 355(b) the proportion of all the outstanding stock required to adopt the amendment` `the proportion of all the outstanding stock by which the certificate specifically authorizes such an amendment, if it does` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proportion of all the outstanding stock by which the certificate specifically authorizes such an amendment, if it does`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 1
    WHEN JUST authorized THEN (IF authorized AT LEAST (2 DIVIDED BY 3) THEN authorized ELSE 1)

-- src:1774 | (b) If the certificate of incorporation as originally filed does not contain a provision authorized by subsection (a) of this section, the certificate may be amended to include such provision if adopted by the affirmative vote of the holders of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote, unless the certificate of incorporation specifically authorizes such an amendment by a vote which shall be not less than 2/3 of all the outstanding stock whether or not entitled to vote.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 355(b) (src:1774)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation as originally filed does not contain a provision authorized by s 355(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proportion of all the outstanding stock by which the certificate specifically authorizes such an amendment, if it does` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote, cast for the amendment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355(b) the amendment adding the option to dissolve is adopted` `the certificate of incorporation as originally filed does not contain a provision authorized by s 355(a)` `the proportion of all the outstanding stock by which the certificate specifically authorizes such an amendment, if it does` `the number of votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote, cast for the amendment` `the number of votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation as originally filed does not contain a provision authorized by s 355(a)`
    THEN `the vote carries` (`at least` (`s 355(b) the proportion of all the outstanding stock required to adopt the amendment` `the proportion of all the outstanding stock by which the certificate specifically authorizes such an amendment, if it does`) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote")) `the number of votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote, cast for the amendment` `the number of votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 356 Effect of this subchapter on other laws`

-- A corporation that is not a close corporation is outside the subchapter's effect; for a corporation organized under
-- the chapter that is not a close corporation, the subchapter repeals no statute or rule of law applicable to it.
-- src:1779 | This subchapter shall not be deemed to repeal any statute or rule of law which is or would be applicable to any corporation which is organized under this chapter but is not a close corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 356 (src:1779)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356 this subchapter repeals a statute or rule of law applicable to the corporation` `the corporation is organized under this chapter` `the corporation is a close corporation` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is organized under this chapter` AND (NOT `the corporation is a close corporation`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
